          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "il était une fois — \"once upon a time\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il était une fois une petite fille qui vivait dans la forêt. Once upon a time there was a little girl who lived in the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opening of most fairy tales. Literally 'there was one time'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fois is inherited from Latin vicēs \"turns, times\" (Lewis & Short); était is a form of être, whose imperfect is inherited from Latin stāre \"to stand\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
